==Battleground==
*1 [[Metal Doge]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Metal Doge]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 30~33.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*3 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn after 106.67 seconds<sup>3,200f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*3 [[Metal One Horn]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*1 [[St. Dober]] spawns as the boss after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
As with every St. Dober stage, this level boils down to preventing him from doing anything with control debuffs. Except this time it's more difficult because Dober spawns on a timer here, meaning you're hardpressed for cash.

Take care of the initial Metal Doge and Gabriel, then send out someone like [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Soba Cat]] to kill the first Metal One Horn. Once that's done, lure St. Dober to the base to stall with crowd controllers like [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] or [[Juliet Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Juliet the Maiko]] and try to quickly cripple or defeat that dog from hell. When Metal One Horn appears, do your best to ensure it dies as quickly as possible. The peons will be consistently trying to mess you up, be wary.

==Trivia==
*The "Alkilinity" part in BCEN isn't a word. However, the original Japanese stage name presents it as ''[[wikipedia:Alkalinity|alkalinity]]'', which refers to a water body's capacity to resist acidification; it can be assumed that the other part of this stage's name refers to the diversity of aquatic creatures, which also ties in with the sub-chapter name that parodies "Diversity".

